From 20aa69630e40298d7a36f1cb84ddf458dd243eda Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 21:22:22 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] net: carry P2P messages on WebTransport class streams

Attach inbound and outbound sessions to CConnman with QuicPeerSock. Frame,
split and compress messages per class, expose transport statistics, apply
pins/permissions, honor IP-family policy and -listen=0, and shut down the
engine after its node sockets. Retain early CONTROL frames until all five
stream prefixes arrive so a version message cannot disappear in that race.
Bound frame declarations and suppress late-notification SIGPIPE.

Add focused socket/framing/fuzz and node relay/TLS tests. An explicitly
supplied test observer copies bounded public TLS handshake messages without
changing policy, installing a default callback or exporting secrets. Ship
unprivileged capture/JA4 comparison tooling and a handshake-only browser page
for the fingerprint/proxy acceptance extension; profiles remain unmodified.

Evidence: Chronik-enabled daemon and unit builds pass (158/179 actual
incremental actions). The three selected suites pass 26 cases, including
an inert opt-in browser capture helper; the refined domain-SNI observer
passes 75 assertions. Basic pinned WT propagation of 101 blocks plus a
transaction, disconnect/reconnect, and TLS pin/reload tests pass. Chrome
155 passes two isolated authenticated handshake/clean-close captures. The
initial Firefox cutoff is preserved; one corrected fresh-profile run passes
authenticated WT and clean close. Actual node, Chrome and Firefox JA4/raw-field
differences are retained, without
claiming browser equivalence.

Not run: full unit/functional sweeps, the new fuzz target, Linux GSO,
Guix reproducibility, Windows, sanitizers, Safari, reverse-proxy captures,
loss/CPU measurements or soak. W7-W12 and their default-enablement gate
remain unfinished; both defaults stay off.

Coordinator ordered integration (2026-10-20):
Existing causal fixes and mechanical namespace/format adaptations are folded at their first responsible owner. Exact inputs and prefix adaptations are recorded in integration-next final delivery; original author provenance is retained.
